# CharityHub Backend — Deep Audit Report

> **Scope**: Backend only. No frontend changes.  
> **Date**: 2026-02-24  
> **Audited layers**: Prisma schema · Routes · Controllers · Services · Middleware · Config · Env

---

## Executive Summary

The backend has a **fundamental runtime breakage**: the controllers were written against a **different Prisma schema** than the one that exists on disk. Every CRUD endpoint for `members`, `medical`, `income`, and `expenses` will throw a Prisma runtime error (`TypeError: prisma.X is not a function`) because the Prisma models they reference **do not exist**. Additionally, the [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) contains a plain-text weak JWT secret. The server can start, but almost every protected route is broken at runtime.

---

## 🔴 CRITICAL

### C-1 — Schema / Controller Mismatch (System-wide Breakage)

The schema defines these models:
[Family](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#35-207), `Person`, [Income](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js#198-219), `MedicalCase`, `EducationRecord`, `Assistance`, `Scoring`, `ScoringRule`, [Role](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/rbac/rbacService.js#168-183), [Permission](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/rbac/rbacService.js#120-135), `RolePermission`, [User](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js#144-158), `AuditLog`

But the controllers reference models **that do not exist in the schema**:

| Controller | References | Schema Reality |
|---|---|---|
| [members.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/members/members.controller.js) | `prisma.member` | No [Member](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js#79-87) model — use `prisma.person` |
| [members.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/members/members.controller.js) | `medicalRecords`, `educationalTracks` | No such relations — schema has `medicalCases`, `educationRecords` |
| [income.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js) | `prisma.incomeSource` | No `IncomeSource` model — use `prisma.income` |
| [medical.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/medical/medical.controller.js) | `prisma.medicalRecord`, `prisma.member` | No such models — use `prisma.medicalCase`, `prisma.person` |
| [expenses.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/expenses/expenses.controller.js) | `prisma.expense` | **No `Expense` model at all** in schema |
| [families.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js) (list/create) | `members`, `incomeSources`, `expenses` as includes | None of these relation names exist on [Family](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#35-207) |
| [families.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js) (list) | `head_name`, `national_id` filter | No such fields on [Family](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#35-207) model |
| [medicalEligibilityService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js) | `prisma.member`, `family.national_id`, `family.head_name` | Wrong model and non-existent fields |
| [scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js) (line 14) | `const AppError = require(...)` | Imports destructured but uses as `new AppError(...)` — wrong destructure pattern |
| [medicalEligibilityService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js) (line 408) | `prisma.medicalRecord` | Should be `prisma.medicalCase` |

**Impact**: Every request to `/api/v1/members/*`, `/api/v1/income/*`, `/api/v1/expenses/*`, `/api/v1/medical/*` will **crash** with a Prisma error at runtime.

---

### C-2 — Weak, Hardcoded JWT Secret in [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env)

**File**: [backend/.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) line 3

```
JWT_SECRET=charityhub-secret-key-2024
```

- The secret is short, predictable, and committed to the repository.
- Tokens can be **forged offline** by anyone who sees this (e.g. via git history).
- Also: [config/env.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/config/env.js) does **not** list `JWT_SECRET` as a required variable — so it silently falls back to `undefined` in production if [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) is missing, and `jwt.sign` will still sign with `undefined` (valid but insecure).

---

### C-3 — [families.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js) — Unsafe Mass Assignment in [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132)

**File**: [families.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js) lines 186–196

```js
const data = req.body          // ← raw, unvalidated
await prisma.family.update({
  where: { id },
  data,                        // ← entire body passed directly to Prisma
  ...
})
```

An attacker who has `UPDATE_FAMILY` permission can overwrite **any column** on the `families` table — including [id](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.validator.js#31-61), internal audit fields, or the `registration_number` unique key, causing conflicts or data corruption. Same pattern exists in [members.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/members/members.controller.js) (line 124) and [income.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js) (line 112) and [expenses.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/expenses/expenses.controller.js) (line 112).

---

### C-4 — [auth.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/middleware/auth.js) Middleware — Development Auth Bypass Left Active

**File**: [middleware/auth.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/middleware/auth.js) lines 28–38

```js
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' && (!process.env.REQUIRE_AUTH || process.env.REQUIRE_AUTH === 'false')) {
  // Inject fake admin user — authentication BYPASSED
  req.user = { userId: 'dev-user', role: 'Admin', permissions: ALL_PERMISSIONS }
  return next()
}
```

- The [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) has `NODE_ENV=development`, so **all routes are currently publicly accessible** without any token.
- If this server is ever exposed (staging, demo, shared environment), it is **fully open** — no auth required for `DELETE /api/v1/families/:id` etc.
- `REQUIRE_AUTH` is not documented and not listed as a required env var.

---

### C-5 — [scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js) — Wrong Import of [AppError](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js#10-22)

**File**: [services/scoring/scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js) line 14

```js
const AppError = require('../../utils/errors')
// Used as: throw new AppError('...', 400, '...')
```

[utils/errors.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js) exports an **object** `{ AppError, ValidationError, ... }`, not the class directly.  
This means [AppError](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js#10-22) here is the module exports object, not the class. Any `throw new AppError(...)` in this file will throw `TypeError: AppError is not a constructor` at runtime the first time a scoring error occurs (e.g., bad familyId).

---

## 🟠 HIGH

### H-1 — [families.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js) — PMT Scoring Called Inside Transaction but Uses External DB Reads

**File**: [families.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js) lines 167–182

```js
return prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  // ... creates Family, Persons, Incomes ...
  const scoringResult = await calculateFamilyScore(createdFamily.id) // ← uses prisma, NOT tx
})
```

[calculateFamilyScore](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js#303-426) uses the **global [prisma](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/prisma/schema.prisma) client**, not the transaction client `tx`. The newly created records are **not yet committed** when scoring queries run, so `persons` and `incomes` will return empty arrays. The PMT score at registration will always be **0 / baseline** — it will never reflect what was just submitted.

---

### H-2 — PMT Score Not Recalculated on Update

When income, members, or medical data changes, **no scoring recalculation is triggered**. The `Scoring` table will hold stale data indefinitely. The only place score is persisted is inside [registerFamily](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#35-207). There is no `PATCH /families/:id/recalculate` or any trigger-on-update mechanism.

---

### H-3 — [medical.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/medical/medical.controller.js) — Medical Rules Duplicated and Hardcoded

Two separate places calculate the `next_allowed_date` interval logic:
1. [medical.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/medical/medical.controller.js) (lines 108–122, create; lines 177–193, update)
2. [medicalEligibilityService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js) (correct, modular)

The controller does this manually:

```js
let daysInterval = 90 // Category A default
if (data.medical_category === 'B') daysInterval = 60
if (data.medical_category === 'C') daysInterval = 30
if (data.chronic === true) daysInterval -= 10
```

But the same logic also uses string literals (`'B'`, `'C'`) instead of enum values, and **doesn't handle `category D`** (which exists in the schema's `MedicalCategory` enum). The controller logic and the service are out of sync.

---

### H-4 — [logout](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.controller.js#71-87) Route Has No Auth — Token Blacklisting Impossible

**File**: [auth.routes.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.routes.js) line 14

```js
router.post('/logout', authController.logout)  // No requireAuth
```

The logout endpoint is **public** and does nothing (just returns 200). JWTs are never invalidated. A stolen token with 24h TTL stays valid forever after "logout". There is no token blacklist, no refresh token rotation, no short expiry enforcement.

---

### H-5 — Error Handler Leaks Internal Stack Traces in Env Without Explicit Guard

**File**: [middleware/errorHandler.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/middleware/errorHandler.js) line 25

```js
...(process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' && { stack: err.stack }),
```

Since [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) sets `NODE_ENV=development`, stack traces are always leaked. If this server is used in any shared/demo environment without changing `NODE_ENV`, error responses expose full stack traces to end users.

---

### H-6 — [auth.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js) — Redundant DB Query on Login

**File**: [auth.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js) lines 86–124

```js
const user = await prisma.user.findUnique(...)           // query 1: get user
const userWithPermissions = await getUserWithPermissions(user.id) // query 2: get same user again
await prisma.user.update({ where: { id: user.id }, data: {} })   // query 3: empty update
```

Login performs **3 database queries** (one of which is entirely empty — `data: {}`). The empty [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132) is a dead code stub that was never finished but consumes a DB round-trip on every login.

---

### H-7 — `expenses` Module Has No Schema Model

The entire `expenses` module (controller + routes) operates on `prisma.expense` / `prisma.expense.findMany` / `prisma.expense.create` — but the Prisma schema has **no `Expense` model at all**. There is no corresponding table, no migration for it, and no relation on [Family](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#35-207). This module is dead code that will always throw at runtime.

---

## 🟡 MEDIUM

### M-1 — [families.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js) [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179) Action Duplicates [register](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#12-37) Logic

There are **two** family creation flows:  
- `POST /api/v1/families/register` — uses [families.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js) (transactional, with scoring)  
- `POST /api/v1/families` — uses inline `prisma.family.create` in the controller (no transaction, no scoring, no related data)

This creates two inconsistent code paths for the same operation. The [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179) controller uses `prisma.family` fields like `head_name`, `national_id`, `spouse_name`, `classification`, `status` — **none of which exist in the Prisma schema**. It will fail silently with a Prisma validation error.

---

### M-2 — No Input Validation on Most Controllers

Only two validators exist:
- [families.validator.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.validator.js) (Joi — good, only used in [register](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#12-37))
- [auth.validator.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.validator.js) (Joi — good, only used in [login](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js#78-143))

**Unvalidated controllers** (raw `req.body` passed directly to Prisma):
- [members.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/members/members.controller.js) — [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179), [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132)
- [income.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js) — [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179), [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132) (partial: only `amount` is parsed)
- [expenses.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/expenses/expenses.controller.js) — [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179), [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132)
- [medical.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/medical/medical.controller.js) — [create](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.controller.js#118-179), [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132)

This means **any payload shape** can be sent to these endpoints. Prisma will silently ignore unknown fields but known fields like `family_id` or `person_id` can be overridden by the client.

---

### M-3 — No Rate Limiting Applied

`express-rate-limit` is in [package.json](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/package.json) but **never imported or applied** anywhere in [app.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/app.js) or any route file. The login endpoint has no brute-force protection. High-value endpoints (scoring batch, registration) have no throttling.

---

### M-4 — No Pagination on Sub-resource Endpoints

`members` list, `income` list, `expenses` list, `medical` list all use `findMany` with **no `take`/`skip` limit**. A family with thousands of records will load everything in memory. The `families` list route paginates, but sub-resources don't.

---

### M-5 — Missing UUID Validation on Route Parameters

Route params like [/:id](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.validator.js#31-61), `/:familyId`, `/:memberId` accept **any string**. There is no middleware or guard that validates the param is a valid UUID before hitting Prisma. Prisma will throw `PrismaClientValidationError` (not a clean 400) if a non-UUID is passed.

---

### M-6 — `ScoringRule` Table Is Never Seeded, Scoring Falls Back Silently

**File**: [scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js) lines 225–246

```js
if (!rule) {
  console.warn(`ScoringRule '${ruleKey}' not found. Using default: 1.0`)
  return 1.0
}
```

[prisma/seed.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/prisma/seed.js) does not seed any `ScoringRule` records. Every scoring call silently falls back to coefficient `1.0`. There is no admin UI, no migration, and no documentation for managing coefficients.

---

### M-7 — [medicalEligibilityService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js) — N+1 Query Pattern

**File**: [medicalEligibilityService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js) lines 323–340

```js
const memberEvaluations = await Promise.all(
  family.members.map((member) => {
    if (member.medicalRecords && member.medicalRecords.length > 0) {
      return evaluateMemberMedicalEligibility(member.id, currentDate) // ← re-queries DB per member
    }
  })
)
```

The family was already loaded with all `members` and `medicalRecords` in the outer query. But [evaluateMemberMedicalEligibility](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js#178-275) then issues **another DB query per member** (`prisma.member.findUnique`). For a family with 6 members, this is 1 + 6 = 7 queries instead of 1.

---

### M-8 — [ForbiddenError](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js#44-49) Constructor Signature Inconsistency

**File**: [utils/errors.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js) lines 44–48 and [middleware/rbac.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/middleware/rbac.js) line 27

[ForbiddenError](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js#44-49) constructor signature is [(message, details)](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/medical/medical.controller.js#10-55) but [requirePermission](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/middleware/rbac.js#11-60) calls it as:
```js
new ForbiddenError(message, statusCode, 'PERMISSION_DENIED', { requiredPermission })
```
The second argument is passed as `details` (object), but `401` (a number) is being passed — `statusCode` is silently discarded. The error always returns `403` regardless of intent from the caller's perspective.

---

### M-9 — [auth.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js) — JWT Secret Not Validated at Startup, Fallback to `undefined`

**File**: [config/env.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/config/env.js) line 24

```js
jwt: {
  secret: process.env.JWT_SECRET || process.env.JWT_ACCESS_SECRET,
```

`JWT_SECRET` is NOT in `requiredVars`. If both are undefined, `config.jwt.secret` is `undefined`. `jwt.sign(payload, undefined)` will throw `secretOrPrivateKey must have a value`. This will silently crash auth at runtime in environments missing the env var.

---

## 🔵 LOW / Code Smells

### L-1 — Duplicate SIGINT/SIGTERM Handlers

[config/prisma.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/config/prisma.js) registers `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` handlers. [server.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/server.js) also registers them via [gracefulShutdown](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/server.js#22-39). There are **two separate `prisma.$disconnect()` calls** on the same signal — risk of double-disconnect errors on shutdown.

---

### L-2 — Dead Code: Empty [update](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js#100-132) in [auth.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.js)

```js
await prisma.user.update({
  where: { id: user.id },
  data: {
    // Add lastLoginAt field if exists in schema
  },
})
```
Every login performs a DB `UPDATE` with an **empty `data` object**. This will either error or be a no-op depending on Prisma version, but is always a wasted round-trip.

---

### L-3 — Health Check Duplicated

`/api/health` exists in [app.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/app.js) AND `/api/v1/health` exists in [routes/api.v1.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/routes/api.v1.js). Two health checks, inconsistent paths.

---

### L-4 — [mapClassificationToEnum](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js#17-34) in [families.service.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.service.js) — Missing FRAGILE Case

```js
function mapClassificationToEnum(code) {
  switch (code) {
    case 'FRAGILE': return VulnerabilityClassification.VERY_FRAGILE
    case 'WEAK':    return VulnerabilityClassification.WEAK
    case 'MODERATE':return VulnerabilityClassification.MODERATE
    default:        return VulnerabilityClassification.OUT_OF_PRIORITY
  }
}
```

The scoring service returns code `'FRAGILE'` → persisted as `VERY_FRAGILE`. But the classification schema enum also has `FRAGILE` (distinct from `VERY_FRAGILE`). The mapping skips `FRAGILE` enum value — it's unreachable. This may be intentional but is undocumented.

---

### L-5 — `EDUCATION_WEIGHTS` Missing `NURSERY` Level

[scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js) defines `EDUCATION_WEIGHTS` without `NURSERY` key (which exists in the `EducationLevel` schema enum). Falls back to `NONE` weight silently.

---

### L-6 — [income.controller.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/income/income.controller.js) — `reduce` on Decimal Type Will Lose Precision

```js
const total = incomeSources.reduce((sum, source) => {
  return sum + parseFloat(source.amount)
}, 0)
```

`amount` is `Decimal` (Prisma). `parseFloat` on a Decimal object calls `.toString()` first — this is safe, but floating-point accumulation is used for a currency total that should use integer arithmetic (cents) or a Decimal library.

---

### L-7 — No Audit Log Writes

The `AuditLog` model exists in the schema with a full design (table_name, record_id, action, old_data, new_data, changed_by). But **no code anywhere writes to it**. The `audit.enabled` config flag exists in [env.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/config/env.js) but is never read. The RBAC roles include `VIEW_AUDIT_LOG` permission but there is no route to read audit logs.

---

### L-8 — [families.routes.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/modules/families/families.routes.js) — Wrong Permission for Family List/Read

```js
router.get('/', requirePermission('VIEW_SCORING'), ...)
router.get('/:id', requirePermission('VIEW_SCORING'), ...)
```

Using `VIEW_SCORING` to guard basic family read access couples two unrelated concerns. A `VIEW_FAMILY` permission should exist. The `Auditor` role has `VIEW_SCORING` and would see family data, which may not be intended.

---

### L-9 — No `.env.example` File

Only [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) exists (with real credentials and weak secret). There is no `.env.example` for new developers, and the real [.env](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/.env) with production-adjacent secrets is likely tracked in git.

---

## Summary Table

| Severity | Count | Key Issues |
|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Critical | 5 | Schema/controller mismatch breaks all sub-resource endpoints, weak JWT, mass assignment, auth bypass, wrong AppError import |
| 🟠 High | 7 | Scoring inside transaction won't see new data, stale scores on update, duplicate medical rules, no logout invalidation, stack trace leak, N+1 login queries, missing Expense model |
| 🟡 Medium | 9 | No validation on CRUD, rate limiting installed but never applied, no pagination on sub-resources, no UUID param validation, ScoringRule never seeded, N+1 in eligibility service, ForbiddenError constructor bug, JWT secret not required |
| 🔵 Low | 9 | Duplicate signal handlers, dead code, duplicated health check, incomplete enum mapping, missing NURSERY education weight, float precision on currency, unused audit log, wrong permission on family read, missing .env.example |

---

## Recommended Fix Priority

1. **Fix all C-1 model name mismatches** (rename controller model references to match schema)
2. **Fix C-5** ([AppError](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/utils/errors.js#10-22) import in [scoringService.js](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js))
3. **Fix H-1** (pass `tx` into [calculateFamilyScore](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/scoring/scoringService.js#303-426) during registration transaction)
4. **Rotate JWT secret** to ≥32 random bytes, add to required env vars
5. **Remove dev auth bypass** or gate it with an explicit flag outside `NODE_ENV`
6. **Add input validation** (Joi schemas) to all CRUD controllers
7. **Apply rate limiting** to `/auth/login` and heavy endpoints
8. **Trigger score recalculation** on income/person/medical update
9. **Fix N+1** in [evaluateFamilyMedicalEligibility](file:///d:/Charity_Hub/backend/src/services/eligibility/medicalEligibilityService.js#276-395)
10. **Centralize medical interval logic** — remove duplicate from controller, use service
